      "text": "គណនាដែនៈ A = lim_{x→π/3} (√(2cosx)-1)/(2cos2x+1)",
      "normalizedText": "Compute limit A = lim_{x→π/3} (√(2cosx)-1)/(2cos2x+1). This is 0/0 form. Multiply numerator and denominator by conjugate, use cos2x = 2cos²x-1 to factor, cancel (2cosx-1), then substitute x=π/3. Answer: A = 1/4.",
      "problem": {
        "textKh": "គណនាដែន A (ទម្រង់ 0/0)",
        "text": "Compute the limit (0/0 indeterminate form)",
        "latex": "A = \\lim_{x\\to\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\frac{\\sqrt{2\\cos x}-1}{2\\cos 2x+1}"
      },
      "solutionSteps": [
        {
          "textKh": "គុណនឹង conjugate នៃ numerator",
          "text": "Multiply top and bottom by conjugate of numerator",
          "latex": "A = \\lim_{x\\to\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\frac{(\\sqrt{2\\cos x}-1)(\\sqrt{2\\cos x}+1)}{(2\\cos 2x+1)(\\sqrt{2\\cos x}+1)}"
        },
        {
          "textKh": "ប្រើ cos2x = 2cos²x - 1 ដើម្បីសំព្រួញ denominator",
          "text": "Use cos2x = 2cos²x-1 to factor denominator",
          "latex": "= \\lim_{x\\to\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\frac{2\\cos x - 1}{(2(2\\cos^2 x-1)+1)(\\sqrt{2\\cos x}+1)} = \\lim_{x\\to\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\frac{2\\cos x-1}{(4\\cos^2 x-1)(\\sqrt{2\\cos x}+1)}"
        },
        {
          "textKh": "ដំឡើង 4cos²x-1 = (2cosx-1)(2cosx+1)",
          "text": "Factor denominator: 4cos²x-1 = (2cosx-1)(2cosx+1)",
          "latex": "= \\lim_{x\\to\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\frac{2\\cos x-1}{(2\\cos x-1)(2\\cos x+1)(\\sqrt{2\\cos x}+1)} = \\lim_{x\\to\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\frac{1}{(2\\cos x+1)(\\sqrt{2\\cos x}+1)}"
        },
        {
          "textKh": "ជំនួស x=π/3: cos(π/3)=1/2",
          "text": "Substitute x=π/3: cos(π/3)=1/2",
          "latex": "A = \\frac{1}{(2\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}+1)(\\sqrt{2\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}}+1)} = \\frac{1}{(1+1)(1+1)} = \\frac{1}{4}"
        }
      ],
      "finalAnswer": {
        "textKh": "A = 1/4",
        "text": "A = 1/4",
        "latex": "A = \\frac{1}{4}"
      },
